    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:EGu">EGu</ref> 7.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="132" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif frigman<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.11"/> freolsdæge wyrce, þolie his freotes oððe gylde wíte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.12"/>, lahslite. Ðeowman<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.13"/> þolie his hyde oððe hydgyldes.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.14"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="132" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf friman freolsdæge wyrce, ðolie his freotes oððe gylde wíte, lahslite. Ðeowman ðolige his hyde oþþe hydgyldes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.star"/><pb n="133" ed="#liebermann"/>Si liber festis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.15"/> diebus operetur, perdat libertatem suam uel reddat witam (aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.16"/>) lahslit. Seruus perdat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.17"/> corium suum uel hidgildum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.18"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="106" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif frigman<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#EGu_7-1.attnote.fn.8"/> freolsdæge wyrce, þolie his freotes oððe gylde wíte, lahslite. Ðeowman þolie his hyde oððe hydgyldes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="6" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif frigman freolsdæge wyrce, þolie his freotes oððe gylde wite oððe lahslite. Ðeowman þolie his hyde oððe hydgyldes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="133" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.de.1"/> ein Freier am Feiertage arbeitet, verliere er seine Freiheit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.de.2"/> oder zahle Strafgeld [bezw.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.de.3"/>] Rechtsbruchbusse.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.de.4"/> Ein Sklav<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#EGu_7-1.lnote.de.5"/> verliere [in diesem Falle] seine Haut oder Hautgeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a free man works on a feast-day, let him lose his freedom or pay a fine [or] the penalty for breach of law. Let a slave [in this case] lose his hide or the hide-money.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="107" ed="#attenborough"/>If a freeman works during a church festival, he shall be reduced to slavery, or pay a fine or <hi rend="italic">lahslit</hi>. A slave shall undergo the lash or pay the fine in lieu thereof.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="7" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If a freeman works on a holy day, he shall forfeit his freedom, or pay a penalty or lahslit. A slave will receive a whipping or pay to redeem himself.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_45-1">II Cn 45.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_45-2">II Cn 45.2</ref>; <ref target="clause:Northu_55">Northu 55</ref>; <ref target="clause:Northu_56">Northu 56</ref>; <ref target="clause:Northu_57">Northu 57</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="58"><label>adapts</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_45-1">II Cn 45.1–47.1</ref> <quote>the secular code adapted the sanctions already provided by the ‘Edward-Guthrum’ tract had for working on feasting days or breaching a fast</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="469"><label>penalty from</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_45-1">II Cn 45.1</ref> <quote>the penalty of healsfang comes from Wihtred II, where Ine 3.2 and “Edward and Guthrum” 7.1 prescribe loss of freedom</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="469"><label>from</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_45-2">II Cn 45.2</ref> <quote>from “Edward and Guthrum”, 7.1, in agreement with Ine 3.1</quote></note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">wite oððe lahslite: wite lahslite BH</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">133</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">De festorum operationibus <hi rend="italic">überschreibt MHk; vgl. Ld zu</hi> 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">De festorum operationibus as heading in MHk; cf. Ld on 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">133</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">op. d. fe. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">op. d. fe. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">133</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">Br; fehlt TMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uel Br; omitted in TMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">133</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. su. p. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> c. p. <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> su. <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. su. p. T; c. p. without su. MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">133</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hyng. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hyng. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">freoman <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">freoman Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þeowe man þolige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þeowe man þolige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hydeg. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hydeg. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Teilweise wörtlich aus Ine 3, 2, der aber vom Sonntag (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3a) spricht. Benutzt in II Cn 45, 1 f. = Hn 11, 10. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Feiertag 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Partly verbatim from Ine 3, 2, who, however, speaks of Sunday (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3a). Used in II Cn 45, 1 f. = Hn 11, 10. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Feiertag 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So nur Ine; Halsfang Wi 11 und Cn = Hn</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Thus only Ine; healsfang Wi 11 and Cn = Hn</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘oder’ in mehreren Hss. des Q ist richtig aus dem Sinne ergänzt. Der Ausdruck ist nur, weil fortwährend am Satzende gleich, hier im Original oder Archetyp gekürzt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘or’ in several MSS of Q is correctly supplied from the sense. The expression has been abbreviated here in the original or archetype only because it is always the same at the end of each sentence</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hinzuzudenken wie <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 2 ‘bei Dänen’; daraus <hi rend="italic">12 or</hi> Northu 56</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">To be understood, as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 2: ‘among the Danes’; hence <hi rend="italic">12 or</hi> Northu 56</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="EGu_7-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Aus Ine 3, 1. Benutzt in II Cn 45, 2. Northu 56. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> unfrei 15</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">From Ine 3, 1. Used in II Cn 45, 2. Northu 56. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> unfrei 15</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="EGu_7-1.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><label>frigman</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">friman</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">freoman</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
